{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Bless</b> — Because he mentioned the heavens, he mentioned those who dwell in it, and they are the angels, which are not body. For through them the decrees come from the heavens, as in the matter of Sennacherib. And Moses said: <i>and He sent the angel of His Presence and saved them</i> (Isaiah 63:9), and <i>the angel of His Presence saved them</i>." "<b>Mighty in strength</b> — For there is no power in any created being to withstand them, and the angel who came to Jacob was a command." "<b>And the meaning of 'to hear the voice of His word'</b> — For they are not like human beings, who hope for reward from HaShem for doing His word; rather this alone is their reward and their delight and their glory — to hear the voice of His word."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 103, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra cites Moses but quotes Isaiah 63:9; the phrase 'מלאך פניו' appears in that verse and is attributed to Moses as speaker in the prophetic literature. The verse reference is implicit in the Hebrew.", 1 "The phrase 'מצווה היה' is cryptic; rendered hyper-literally. Possibly refers to the angel being 'commanded' (sent under orders), but left untranslated as the syntax is ambiguous."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:38:09.088116475Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}